    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0509" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/630: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Nogales</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Damm</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-10T19:00:00-05:00">April 10, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Please forward following to Consul at Guaymas: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your April 8, 10 p.m.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d459-f1"/> is being
                            telegraphically repeated to Embassy. You will again impress upon rebel
                            authorities principles set out in Department’s March 29, 6 p.m.<anchor
                                n="44" xml:id="d459-f2"/> and inform them that the Government of the
                            United States expects and demands that American life, property, and
                            interests shall receive due and proper protection from all wanton or
                            illegal acts sacrificing or endangering them. Advise Department of
                            action taken.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="43" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Department in telegram of April 8 from the Consul at Nogales
                    (not printed), reporting among other matters: “presumed that he [Manzo] is about
                    to levy on Guaymas but as yet nothing has been done.” (812.00 Sonora/578)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d459-f2" n="44" xml:id="d459-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 217 of the same date to the Ambassador in Mexico, <ref
                        target="#pg373">p. 373</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
